{"text": "Slide 1\nQuillon Robotics, Inc. — Board finance update\nPrepared by Wanjiru Kamande, fractional CFO\nBoard meeting of November 18, 2025 — CONFIDENTIAL\nSpeaker notes: Deck goes only to the three directors. Hollis dials in from Nantucket; send to hollis@grimsbyfo.example, not his assistant.\n\nSlide 2\nCap table (fully diluted) at 10/31/2025\nHolder\tClass\tShares\t%\nKsenia Abramovich (CEO)\tCommon\t3,600,000\t36.0%\nTeodoro Balderas (CTO)\tCommon\t2,900,000\t29.0%\nTessera Seed Partners\tSeed Pref.\t1,500,000\t15.0%\nGrimsby Family Office LP\tSeed Pref.\t1,000,000\t10.0%\nOption pool\tCommon\t1,000,000\t10.0%\nSpeaker notes: Teo never filed his Section 83(b) election in 2022. Counsel says the exposure is his personally, roughly $310,000 of ordinary income at the last 409A price. He does not know we know.\n\nSlide 3\nBridge financing\nConvertible note from Grimsby Family Office: $750,000, 8%, matures May 31, 2026\nTessera will match up to $500K if the pilot signs by 12/15\nWire received 11/04/25, ref FT25308-004417\nSpeaker notes: Hollis Grimsby asked for a personal guarantee from Ksenia. She refused. He then asked for a board seat for his son-in-law. Not on the agenda; expect it under other business.\n\nSlide 4\nCash and runway\nOperating account, Monadnock Commerce Bank, ending 7714: $1,184,220\nMonthly net burn: $162,000 — runway about seven months with the note\nPayroll: 11 people, $118,400 per month fully loaded\nCompany card (Amex ending 9204): $14,870 in October, mostly cloud compute\nSpeaker notes: Online banking is still under Ksenia's login only (kabramovich_qr). I need my own credentials before year end.\n\nSlide 5\n409A and option grants\nNew 409A from Ahluwalia Valuation Advisors (Sandeep Ahluwalia) dated October 20, 2025: $0.41 per common share\nFee: $4,500. Grants to four engineers to be approved today.\nSpeaker notes: ASC 718 expense for the new grants is immaterial this year.\n\nSlide 6\nFounder matters (closed session)\nK. Abramovich: work authorization\nT. Balderas: leave of absence request\nSpeaker notes: Ksenia is on an O-1 visa that expires in March; the green card petition (receipt IOE0924418820) is pending. If it is denied she cannot remain CEO in the US. Budget $18,000 for premium processing and counsel. Teo has asked for eight weeks off from January. He told me in confidence he is starting treatment for alcohol dependence and his divorce is being finalized; his wife's lawyer has already written asking about his 2,900,000 shares. Nothing in writing to the full board, please.", "kind": "PowerPoint presentation", "detail": "6 slides · 394 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Wanjiru Kamande", "Hollis", "Ksenia Abramovich", "Teodoro Balderas", "Sandeep Ahluwalia", "K. Abramovich", "T. Balderas", "Ksenia", "Teo"], "companies": ["Quillon Robotics, Inc.", "Cap table", "Grimsby Family Office", "Tessera Seed Partners", "Monadnock Commerce Bank", "Ahluwalia Valuation Advisors"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Nantucket"], "health": ["alcohol dependence", "divorce"], "sensitive": ["Ksenia Kamande", "Teodoro Balderas", "Grimsby Family Office LP", "Hollis Grimsby", "O-1 visa", "green card"], "names": ["Wanjiru", "Teodoro", "Hollis", "Sandeep", "K.", "T.", "Ksenia", "Teo"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 2.8000000044703484, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 8, "end": 30, "text": "Quillon Robotics, Inc.", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Quillon Robotics, Inc."}, {"start": 66, "end": 81, "text": "Wanjiru Kamande", "kind": "person", "source"